RF.put("questb:b6",{"8566":{"id":8566,"t":"Past Victories in Arathi","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Arathi Resource Crate","desc":"Ah, yes! Of course we wouldn't forget about your past accomplishments in Arathi Basin.","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor\nLevel 1 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 4 6 Side Horde Shareable Yes Quest ID 8566","cats":["arathi-basin"]},"8166":{"id":8166,"t":"The Battle for Arathi Basin!","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Assault the mine, the lumber mill, the blacksmith and the farm, then return to Field Marshal Oslight in Refuge Pointe.\nMine Assaulted\nLumber Mill Assaulted\nBlacksmith Assaulted\nFarm Assaulted","desc":"‹name›, the battle for Arathi Basin is a battle for resources and territory. Key points in the area must be held and operated in order to supply our forces with much needed raw materials and supplies. I charge you to assault the points farthest from our Arathi Basin base.\nAssault the farm, the mine, the lumber mill and the blacksmith when they are controlled by the enemy. Find the enemy's banner and rip it from its flag post!\nWhen you have done this to all four points, return to me.","rew":"Money: 1 30 1 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+200 reputation with The League of Arathor","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":45.8,"y":45.5,"n":"Field Marshal Oslight","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"646":{"id":646,"t":"Trol'kalar","lv":42,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Trol'kalar to Zengu in Hammerfall.\nSheathed Trol'kalar\nProvided: Sheathed Trol'kalar","desc":"The light slowly fades, the sword Trol'kalar, held within a stone sheath has been released.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBlood-tinged Armor Pit Fighter's Shield\nExperience: 4,300\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"‹name›! Have you taken the sword?","done":"For generations, the forces of Strom and Arathor ravaged the trolls. Now their greatest weapon is in our hands. Our inching progress in the steamy forests of Zul'Gurub will be no more.\nYour assistance has been great, ‹name›, and the Darkspear trolls are indebted to you.\nI will be sure that the sword is delivered to Nimboya at Grom'gol.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":28.9,"y":59.6,"n":"Trollbane's Tomb","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.8,"y":34,"n":"Zengu","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1046":{"id":1046,"t":"Raene's Cleansing","lv":30,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Replica Dartol's Rod of Transformation.","obj":"Bring Ran Bloodtooth's Skull and Dartol's Rod of Transformation to Raene Wolfrunner in Astranaar.\nRan Bloodtooth's Skull Ran Bloodtooth\nDartol's Rod of Transformation\nProvided: Ran Bloodtooth's Skull","desc":"Return to your own tribe and let them know of your victory here.\nShow them your trophy, and bask in the glory...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGlacial Stone Gutterblade\nNew in Forever: Replica Dartol's Rod of Transformation.\nYou will also receive:\nRing of Pure Silver Replica Dartol's Rod of Transformation\nExperience: 3,050\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The Sentinels do what they can here in Ashenvale, but it's thanks to ‹race›s like you that we have gained the ground we have.","done":"So, this is the skull of the fiercest furbolg threat in Ashenvale?\nI am more than pleased with your abilities, ‹name›. The Sentinels cannot thank you enough. I hope we can rely on you again in the future to help our people.\nI shall put this skull and Dartol's Rod in a place of reverence for others to see.\nTeronis would be proud. Thank you again.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":50.8,"y":75.1,"n":"Krolg","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":36.6,"y":49.6,"n":"Raene Wolfrunner","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"726":{"id":726,"t":"Passing Word of a Threat","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Historian Karnik.","desc":"<Advisor Belgrum reaches the end of the note, and his eyes widen for a moment.>\nOch, these are evil tidings.\n‹name›, please return to Historian Karnik and tell him on the king's authority to act on this information swiftly and decisively. He must halt the Shadowforge's activities in the Badlands.","rew":"Experience: 2,350\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","done":"You're treating this matter with an urgency I'd expect from the king himself, ‹name›.\nAll right, then. I know what'll bring the Shadowforge down.\nTheir presence in Uldaman can be slowed if we strike them at their base of operations: Angor Fortress.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":22.6,"n":"Advisor Belgrum","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":23,"n":"Historian Karnik","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"8966":{"id":8966,"t":"The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Brazier of Beckoning to summon forth the spirit of Mor Grayhoof and slay him. Return to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain with the Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet and the Brazier of Beckoning.\nLeft Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet Mor Grayhoof , Isalien , Jarien , Sothos and 1 more\nBrazier of Beckoning\nMor Grayhoof slain\nProvided: Brazier of Beckoning","desc":"My friend, Mor Grayhoof, was the first to fall victim to possession of a piece of Lord Valthalak's amulet, and the corrupting spirit fragment that it contains. After stealing Valthalak's spellbook and amulet, we fled for our lives from the upper portion of Blackrock Spire. Along the way, Mor fell into the lower portion of the spire.\nLater, we discovered that he survived the fall, only to be captured and tortured by War Master Voone. A few spectral assassins snuck in and slew him right in front of Voone.","rew":"Experience: 8,300","back":"Then it is done? You have retrieved the left piece of Lord Valthalak's amulet and finally put to rest the spirit of my old companion, Mor Grayhoof?","done":"You have done a great thing, ‹name›. One spirit rests in peace, but there is still much work to be done before we can put all of this behind us.\nUnfortunately, I do not know the location of the one who died with the right piece of the amulet in their possession. But do not fear; in life I was a dabbler in the art of divination, so I have another task for you, which is going to enable us to ferret out the final piece.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"4726":{"id":4726,"t":"Broodling Essence","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Broodling Essence and the Draco-Incarcinatrix 900 to Tinkee Steamboil at the Flame Crest in the Burning Steppes.\n8 Broodling Essence Broodling Essence\nDraco-Incarcinatrix 900\nProvided: Draco-Incarcinatrix 900","desc":"I have been studying the dragonkin of the Burning Steppes for weeks, and I think I've finally had a breakthrough! I created a device--I call it the Draco Incarcinatrix 900. It can capture the essence of dragon whelp broodlings!\nOr, at least I think it can.\nHere, take the device and zap a broodling in the Burning Steppes with it. While it's under the device's effects, defeat the broodling and its essence should be released.\nIf it is, then splendid! Bring me back samples so I can study them!","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"Do you have the broodling essence, ‹name›? I can't wait to study it.\nAnd besides that... my patron is not the type of person you want to disappoint.","done":"It worked! You got the essence! Well done, ‹name›! Well done!\nThis essence will be invaluable in my research. I hope to one day learn how to capture living dragons whelps, or perhaps capture their eggs. If I could find a way to do that, then I would be the envy of dragon scholars around the world!\nMy employer would also be happy, and as I said before, he's someone you want to keep happy...","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65.2,"y":24,"n":"Tinkee Steamboil","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"96646":{"id":96646,"t":"Camping 101 cooking","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Zerril Softbreeze in Shen'dar Village to learn to become a cook.\nLearn cooking from Zerril Softbreeze in Shen'dar Village","desc":"So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, ‹class›. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.","back":"A good campfire is the foundation to any good camp.","done":"With this, you'll be able to set up a camp anywhere out in the wilderness. What you've learned is just the basics, so you won't be able to place too many furnishings around it.\nRaise your cooking skill and you might just be able to learn to make even bigger fires.\nYou can also learn the basics of furnishing your campsites from other tradeskill trainers if you're savvy in their skills.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.8,"y":43.8,"n":"Zerril Softbreeze","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94326":{"id":94326,"t":"Craftsmans writ radiant belt","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Radiant Belt\nRadiant Belt","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Radiant Belt, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Radiant Belt Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94326","cats":["crafting"]},"94246":{"id":94246,"t":"Craftsmans writ red whelp gloves","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Red Whelp Gloves\nRed Whelp Gloves","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Red Whelp Gloves, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Red Whelp Gloves Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94246","cats":["crafting"]},"97926":{"id":97926,"t":"Making do","lv":17,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Alexston's Reply to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine in Darkshore.\nProvided: Alexston's Reply","desc":"I wish it was that easy to help, ‹class›. I really do.\nShould you choose to spend more time in our lands, you will find that many are without. Stormwind's coffers are not what they once were, and what remains is spread thin.\nGive this reply to the elder the next time you see him. It's not what he's hoping for, but it's all I have to offer right now.","rew":"You will receive:\nShipwright's Satchel\nMoney: 90 0 gold, 0 silver, 90 copper Experience: 130","back":"You have returned. What news comes from Stormwind?","done":"Sad news indeed. Still, I thank you for making the journey.\nWith neither Stormwind nor Darnassus coming to aid us, it seems that Auberdine's fate is our own to decide.\nStormwind City Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49,"y":30.2,"n":"Baros Alexston","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":40.2,"n":"Thundris Windweaver","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"966":{"id":966,"t":"The Tower of Althalaxx","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 4 Worn Parchments for Balthule Shadowstrike near the Tower of Althalaxx.\n4 Worn Parchment Dark Strand Fanatic 45 %","desc":"A group of warlocks has taken up residence around and inside the tower. I would have returned to Auberdine to report to Elissa earlier, but I was afraid that I might miss something while I was away.\nDelgren suspected such a company might be gathering at the tower, but did not know why.\nA few scraps of parchment that the warlocks carry have found their way to my hands, but I need more to complete the puzzle. I warn you not to venture into the tower, however, the warlocks there are much more powerful!","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Have you found any more of their scrolls? I should be able to piece together a larger picture of the cult if you can find them.","done":"Many thanks, ‹name›. This should shed some light on this warlocks' gathering...\nHmm... the Cult of the Dark Strand... I have never heard of this group before. Having no knowledge of their history, it is all but impossible to say what their plans must be.\nThere is no more time to delay. Warning must be delivered to Delgren immediately.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":55,"y":24.9,"n":"Balthule Shadowstrike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"1366":{"id":1366,"t":"Centaur Bounty","lv":31,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 15 Centaur Ears to Felgur Twocuts in Desolace.\n15 Centaur Ear Kolkar Ambusher 20 % , Kolkar Waylayer 20 % , Outcast Necromancer 20 % , Maraudine Khan Advisor 20 % and 4 more","desc":"Now that you scared the centaur clans, it's time to bleed them. When traveling Desolace, hunt centaur. I don't care which clan you hunt. Just gather ears. A hoard of ears.\nBy weakening their numbers you will weaken their resolve, and stamp out any thoughts of expansion.\nGood hunting, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLilac Sash Braced Handguards\nExperience: 3,750\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"How is your collection of ears, ‹name›? Large?","done":"By now, the centaur must know your name. I'm sure they know it, and respect it, and fear it. And just as they know you, they know the banner under which you ride.\nThe banner of the Horde.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":56.2,"y":59.6,"n":"Felgur Twocuts","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"5926":{"id":5926,"t":"Heeding the Call","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise of Thunder Bluff.","desc":"Excuse me, friend...\nIt has come to my attention that Turak Runetotem has put out word that he wishes to speak with you. It seems that your training as a druid is about to take on a new life, and he will be training you personally. Turak is one of the Arch Druid's assistants; he is known as a wise and patient druid, and he should teach you well.\nHe is located in Thunder Bluff, inside the Cenarion Circle's main tent on the Elder Rise.","rew":"Experience: 85\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"I am glad you found your way here today. young ‹class›. The time has come for you to take a large step into a much larger world.\nInside each of Cenarius' children is the call to serve nature. Animals and plants are our friends as well as our charges. We choose to devote our lives as preservers of balance for their sakes as well as our own. Your first step into this world will be to learn of the ways of the bear, and to learn strength of body and heart.\nReady yourself!\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.5,"y":63,"n":"Gennia Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Turak Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"94006":{"id":94006,"t":"The great ursera spirit","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Urs'endris near the falls northeast of Valanaar.","desc":"Greetings, ‹name›. You have progressed in your druidic studies far enough that I think it is time for you to meet one of the great spirits that reside here on Zephras. Urs'endris is a wise and noble spirit, who has taught druids how to take on the ursera shape for generations. Unfortunately his domain has begun to wither and fall into the sky like many other areas of Zephras.\nTo find him, travel northeast near the waterfall in the shadow of the Shrine of Akir. He should be able to instruct you further.","done":"So, you wish to embrace the way of the claw, child? Very well. Let us speak.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":64,"y":75,"n":"Lotheluum Starbreeze","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":69.8,"y":61.6,"n":"Urs'endris","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"98326":{"id":98326,"t":"Frosthowl","lv":9,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay Frosthowl and collect the Sack of Fish for Gretta Ganter in Brewnall Village\nSack of Fish","desc":"Do ye know how hard it is to fish on a frozen lake? My poor husband, Paxton, has been out in the middle of it for days and we barely have a single sack to show fer it.\nWell, we DID have a sack to show fer it. Until the thrice-damned wendigo attacked me and made off with our haul. It'll take us weeks to fish all that back up! If that loudmouth Frosthowl didn't scare 'em all off, anyway.\nDo us a favor and get it back, aye? Drooling brute is hiding somewhere deep in the Grizzled Den to the southeast.","rew":"You will receive:\nFrosthowl's Footwarmers\nMoney: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 775\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"It'll be a hot day in Dun Morogh before I tell Paxton I lost his entire stockpile to a wendigo.","done":"Yer a real lifesaver, Leif!\nMy husband would just laugh it off, but I couldn't bare tellin' him he has to spend another night on the lake. Maybe now we can enjoy a real feast.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":31.4,"y":44.6,"n":"Gretta Ganter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"806":{"id":806,"t":"Dark Storms","lv":12,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Fizzle's Claw to Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill.\nFizzle's Claw Fizzle Darkstorm","desc":"We cannot allow the Burning Blade a foothold in Durotar! We must destroy them before their evil festers!\nI have undergone my own investigations and found that a Burning Blade warlock, the goblin Fizzle Darkstorm, has camped within Thunder Ridge to the northwest. There he and his cultist minions spread chaos.\nFind and defeat Fizzle, and bring me his dead claw!","rew":"You will receive:\nTiger Hide Boots\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Did you find Fizzle, ‹name›? He, and rest of the Burning Blade, must be scoured from our lands!","done":"Aha! You got him!\nYou do your clan proud, ‹name›. And because of you, Durotar is free of one more agent of evil.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52.2,"y":43.2,"n":"Orgnil Soulscar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"1206":{"id":1206,"t":"Jarl Needs Eyes","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Unpopped Darkmist Eyes to \"Swamp Eye\" Jarl at the Swamplight Manor.\n20 Unpopped Darkmist Eye Darkmist Widow , Darkmist Spider , Darkmist Recluse , Darkmist Silkspinner and 1 more","desc":"Eye juice is good juice for drinking. Too bad most critters only have two eyes.\nBut spiders have lots of eyes. Lots and lots. And Darkmist eye juice is tasty. Smooth and salty! Unpopped spider eyes... I taste them already.\nDarkmist spiders are west of here, in the Darkmist Cavern. You figure the spiders are named after the cave... or is it the other way around?","rew":"Experience: 2,750","back":"Where are those eyes?","done":"You got the eyes! You got the eyes! Tasty, tasty spider eyes!\nSome eyes... when you stare at them they stare back. Eat those last. They keep you company... out in the swamp.\nHello, little spider eyes. Hello! You taste like chicken. Gooey, salty chicken!\nMmmh.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":55.4,"y":26.3,"n":"\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"1286":{"id":1286,"t":"The Deserters","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get information about Reethe from Balos Jacken and the deserters in Dustwallow Marsh.","desc":"It has been a struggle maintaining a presence in the marsh, but through strength of our resolve, we have been able to maintain several defensive watchtowers throughout the area.\nThe latest information and scouting reports I have received indicate that a group of deserters has squatted in our abandoned tower at Lost Point, southeast of the inn.\nThe local lieutenant seems to be Balos Jacken. See if you can get some information out of him.\nBe warned, ‹name›. He may be a tough nut to crack.","rew":"Experience: 2,850","done":"Did Vimes send you? Couldn't do his dirty work himself, could he...","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68.2,"y":48.6,"n":"Captain Garran Vimes","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.1,"y":54.3,"n":"Balos Jacken","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5846":{"id":5846,"t":"Of Love and Family","lv":58,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to island of Caer Darrow, in the south-central region of the Plaguelands, and look for any clues as to the whereabouts of the painting.","desc":"When Taelan was a child, we would oft visit Caer Darrow on family excursions. On our last visit, an artist by the name of Renfray painted a portrait of us poised along the beachside. It is my fondest memory of both Taelan and Karandra. For it was at that moment, with my wife and son in my arms, that I felt a bond of love and family that I would never know again.\nIf this painting still exists, you must find it.\nTravel to the ruined island of Caer Darrow and see if the painting or the artist remain.","rew":"Experience: 6,200","done":"How could I forget? Many of the spirits on this island are cursed to relive their last happy memory before they met their tragic end.\nI too am cursed, but not as they - I am one of the few that remembers all...\nPerhaps this thing that you ask me is why I haunt these ruins. Perhaps this thing I tell you shall set me free.\nEastern Plaguelands Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":5.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Tirion Fordring","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":65.8,"y":75.4,"n":"Artist Renfray","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9126":{"id":9126,"t":"Bonescythe Digs","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rohan the Assassin at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 30 Bone Fragments.\n30 Bone Fragments Lord Darkscythe 89.3 % , Skul 57 % in Stratholme , Vectus 50 % in Scholomance , Rattlegore 48 % in Scholomance and 4 more","desc":"Don Julio's Bonescythe armor pattern requires bone fragments - a lot of bone fragments. While those crazy enough to venture into Naxxramas provide me with enough of the core materials to make the armor, I'm always looking for more Scourge bone fragments.\nSo what do you think? Interested in getting your hands dirty and destroying some Scourge at the same time? It's a win-win situation.","rew":"You will receive:\nInsignia of the Crusade\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"I can direct you to skeleton infested locales, ‹class›.","done":"You work fast, ‹name›. Fast like a fox... Say, have I ever told you about the time I was in a barber shop quartet?\nRemind me to tell you that story one of these days.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.9,"n":"Rohan the Assassin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9206":{"id":9206,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Lightning Eel","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 30 Lightning Eel and the Craftsman's Writ - Lightning Eel - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Lightning Eel\n30 Lightning Eel\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Lightning Eel","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order FS-9:\n30 Lightning Eel.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"These make the best eel rolls in the world. That's right - IN THE WORLD.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"5206":{"id":5206,"t":"Marauders of Darrowshire","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Resonating Skulls and the Mystic Crystal to Carlin Redpath in Eastern Plaguelands.\n5 Resonating Skull\nMystic Crystal\nProvided: Mystic Crystal","desc":"Chromie said the relics you gathered are reagents to a powerful spell, and one more is required: skulls from the scourge who took part in the battle of Darrowshire.\nTake this crystal and hunt scourge champions for their skulls. The crystal is enchanted; if a champion took part in the battle, then when you pass the crystal over its skull it will resonate. Bring me those resonating skulls.\nGo, ‹name›. You'll find scourge champions in the Noxious Glade to the north and the Fungal Vale to the west.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Do you have the skulls? Chromie said they will be critical for her spell, and that spell will give us the chance to save Darrowshire.","done":"You found them! Wonderful!\nAlthough I don't fully understand how they can help us, I feel their power and I know in my bones that they are linked to my home village of Darrowshire.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":50,"n":"Carlin Redpath","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"6":{"id":6,"t":"Bounty on Garrick Padfoot","lv":5,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Garrick Padfoot and bring his head to Deputy Willem at Northshire Abbey.\nGarrick's Head Garrick Padfoot","desc":"Garrick Padfoot - a cutthroat who's plagued our farmers and merchants for weeks - was seen at a shack near the vineyards, which lies east of the Abbey and across the bridge. Bring me the villain's head, and earn his bounty!\nBut be wary, ‹name›. Garrick has gathered a gang of thugs around him. He will not be an easy man to reach.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTapered Pants Layered Tunic Ensign Cloak\nExperience: 340\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did you find Garrick's shack? Are we finally free of that villain?","done":"Hah - you caught him! You've done Elwynn a great service, and earned a nice bounty!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.2,"y":42.9,"n":"Deputy Willem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"86":{"id":86,"t":"Pie for Billy","lv":6,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Chunks of Boar Meat to Auntie Bernice Stonefield at the Stonefield's Farm.\n4 Chunk of Boar Meat Dire Mottled Boar 97.7 % , Elder Mottled Boar 82.4 % , Mangy Mountain Boar 81.9 % , Corrupted Mottled Boar 81.6 % and 4 more","desc":"Maybe if I got a pie, I could tell you who has that necklace. And you know, I think that old Bernice lady at that other farm makes great Pork Belly Pies...\nMaybe if you gave her some chunks of boar meat from the boars that hang around our farms, and told her what it was for, she'd bake up a pie for you.","rew":"Experience: 410\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I don't think it's right feeding the boy who stole my necklace in the first place, but if that's what it takes to get back what's mine, then so be it!\nDo you have that boar meat?","done":"Though this wild boar meat is tough, simmer it enough and it sure does make for some tasty pie!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.1,"y":85.7,"n":"Billy Maclure","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":34.5,"y":84.3,"n":"\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3526":{"id":3526,"t":"Goblin Engineering","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you wish to learn more about Goblin Engineering, take the Manual of Engineering Disciplines to Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan.\nManual of Engineering Disciplines\nProvided: Manual of Engineering Disciplines","desc":"Expert engineering yields two distinct disciplines: gnome and goblin. Clearly, goblin engineering is the choice of all brilliant engineers. Learn to master the world through the judicious use of high explosives and fantastic gear!\n‹name›, read this manual. If you want to learn about goblin engineering, then take it to Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan. Remember - membership is permanent and prevents joining the other discipline, so make sure this is what you want before finishing his task.","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"I can smell fresh recruits much like I can an excellent blasting powder - from a mile away. Have you come seeking to learn about the mastery of the explosion?","done":"Well ‹name›, you were wise to seek my tutelage! Any schlep can become an expert at the basics of engineering - the gnomes and their irradiated home of Gnomeregan are proof of that. It takes a strong mind and a steady hand (emphasis on STEADY) though to master the discipline of Goblin Engineering.\nKeep your ears perked ‹name›, and you might learn something.\nUndercity Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":75.3,"y":73.1,"n":"Graham Van Talen","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.3,"n":"Nixx Sprocketspring","e":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"3126":{"id":3126,"t":"Treant Muisek","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 3 Wandering Forest Walkers. Use the Muisek Vessel to shrink and capture the fallen Treants.\n3 Treant Muisek\nTreant Muisek Vessel\nProvided: Treant Muisek Vessel","desc":"The wandering forest walkers that can be found meandering through the forest are our next target, ‹name›. Night elves have enlisted treants as allies to fight against the horde. Their movement may be slow, but their role as protectors is undeniable.\nSoon we will be able to use this power for our own benefit.\nFind 3 wandering forest walkers; kill them, and use the muisek vessel to shrink and capture them.","rew":"Experience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Were you able to capture the wandering forest walkers?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our muisek collection is almost complete.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Witch Doctor Uzer'i","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"566":{"id":566,"t":"WANTED: Baron Vardus","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,150 experience instead of 3,500, 0.9 times as much.","obj":"Kill Baron Vardus and deliver his head to High Executor Darthalia in Tarren Mill.\nHead of Baron Vardus Baron Vardus","desc":"By order of High Executor Darthalia, the human known as Baron Vardus is wanted for crimes against the Forsaken. Vardus is known to be a high-ranking member of the organization known as the Syndicate.\nHe was last spotted in the Uplands in the Alterac Mountains, north of Tarren Mill.\nHe is wanted dead. Bring evidence of his demise to High Executor Darthalia to claim the reward.","rew":"You will receive:\nInferno Robe\nExperience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Ah, ‹name›. Perhaps you've come to collect the bounty on the head of Baron Vardus?","done":"Productive work you do, ‹name›. With Baron Vardus dead, the number of Syndicate leaders grows smaller. Their resistance and irritation will be short-lived.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.6,"y":20.8,"n":"WANTED","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.3,"y":20.5,"n":"High Executor Darthalia","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6086":{"id":6086,"t":"Training the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Belia Thundergranite in Ironforge.","desc":"‹name›, ya now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills ta train it.\nTravel to Ironforge and find the Hall of Arms. There you must speak to one of our most revered animal trainers, Belia Thundergranite. She'll give ya the power to train your new pet, so get goin', lad/lass!\nBelia is a friendly sort; you should have no problems gaining her approval. Good luck, ‹name›.","rew":"You will learn: Training Lesson\nExperience: 420","done":"A new recruit, eh? You're on your way to becoming a great ‹class›, I see.\nYes, I can bestow you with the skills you need to train and guide your pet. Not only will you be able to teach your pet new abilities, you will now be able to feed your pet, as well as revive it, should it fall in battle.\nRemember that the key to getting the most from your new pet is to respect it and treat it well. In turn, your pet will be your most loyal friend.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":45.8,"y":53,"n":"Grif Wildheart","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.5,"y":34.9,"n":"Belia Thundergranite","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"8726":{"id":8726,"t":"Brightspear the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":55.6,"y":43.7,"n":"Elder Brightspear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8646":{"id":8646,"t":"Hammershout the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":36.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Elder Hammershout","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"97286":{"id":97286,"t":"Research access","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","done":"Your actions show you are one who respects knowledge. The library is open for use in your studies.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"7046":{"id":7046,"t":"The Scepter of Celebras","lv":49,"min":41,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Assist Celebras the Redeemed while he creates the Scepter of Celebras.\nSpeak with him when the ritual is complete.","desc":"My scepter was once a source of hope for me. Its power allowed me the freedom to travel quickly through these caverns. I had hoped to bring peace to the spirit of my uncle... It is a task that I now pass to you.\nFor the two parts to once again become one, I will need your assistance in performing the ritual. Please follow me, and listen to my instructions while I channel the energy required to reunite the rod with the diamond.\nTogether, we shall create the Scepter of Celebras once again!","rew":"You will receive:\nScepter of Celebras\nExperience: 5,700","back":"If you wish to restart the ritual, please abandon our first attempt and then speak to me again.","done":"Please take this, and know that the power allotted to you now must be used for good. Continue your journey through the caverns, and with hope, you will find the remains of my uncle. Much danger awaits you, ‹name›.\nSpeak with me again should the need arise.\nDesolace Open the zone on the world map Start Celebras the Redeemed End Celebras the Redeemed Level 49 , requires level 41 Difficulty 41 45 47 52 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 7046\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 49, 9,100 XP in all.\n1 [ 49 ] Legends of Maraudon\nRecover the two parts of the Scepter of Celebras: the Celebrian Rod and the Celebrian Diamond. Find a way to speak with Celebras.\nCavindra Desolace\n3,400 XP\n2 [ 49 ] The Scepter of Celebras this quest\nAssist Celebras the Redeemed while he creates the Scepter of Celebras. Speak with him when the ritual is complete.\nCelebras the Redeemed\n5,700 XP","cats":["maraudon"]},"6646":{"id":6646,"t":"Favor Amongst the Brotherhood, Blood of the Mountain","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Blood of the Mountain Molten Destroyer 7.1 % , Dark Iron Deposit 0.5 % , Molten Giant 0 % , Krom'Grul 0 % and 4 more","back":"The tears of the Fire Lord are a rare find indeed.\nOffer 1 Blood of the Mountain and you shall be granted favor amongst the Brotherhood.","done":"Your offering has been accepted. Favor you have gained. Continue and you shall be allowed access to the ancient trades.\nStart Lokhtos Darkbargainer End Lokhtos Darkbargainer Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6646","cats":["molten-core"]},"5526":{"id":5526,"t":"Shards of the Felvine","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Felvine in Dire Maul and acquire a shard from it. Chances are you'll only be able to procure one with the demise of Alzzin the Wildshaper. Use the Reliquary of Purity to securely seal the shard inside, and return it to Rabine Saturna in Nighthaven, Moonglade.\nSealed Reliquary of Purity\nProvided: Reliquary of Purity","desc":"Your knowledge of Eldre'Thalas - Dire Maul - in Feralas will now come into play, ‹name›. In the eastern part of the ruined city is where Alzzin the Wildshaper has exerted his corrupt dominion. Go there with all due haste and brave whatever challenges await you.\nThe Fruit of Fertility, now corrupted as the Felvine, should be close to Alzzin. When he falls, capture whatever essence of the Felvine you can. Seal it in the Reliquary, and bring it to me.\nGood luck, and Cenarion's speed.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMilli's Shield Milli's Lexicon\nExperience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"With the Sealed Reliquary of Purity in our possession, it will be possible not only to remove a corrupting threat from the world but also to study it under our judicious watch. Perhaps we can even devise new means to combat the taint of corruption that ever threatens Azeroth.\nI know Milli would have had it no other way...","done":"It is done, brave ‹class›, and with that the Cenarion Circle is in your debt. Though the war is far from over, a great battle has been won against those who would bring about our doom.\nPlease - accept this as a token of our enduring gratitude. Know that you are welcomed here as a hero of the Cenarion Circle for your great deed, ‹name›. Thank you.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":51.7,"y":45.1,"n":"Rabine Saturna","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["moonglade"]},"9046":{"id":9046,"t":"Redemption Spaulders","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a pair of Redemption Spaulders if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Spaulders, 12 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 2 Arcanite Bars and 2 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Spaulders Grobbulus 0 % in Naxxramas , Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Patchwerk 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Arcanite Bar\n2 Nexus Crystal","desc":"You will find the remnants of our fallen heroes on the corpses of the Lords of Naxxramas. Bring those desecrated keepsakes to me along with wartorn plate scraps and crafting materials capable of revitalizing the cursed armor and I shall craft a fine piece of armor for you.","rew":"You will receive:\nRedemption Spaulders\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Redemption Spaulders.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"7926":{"id":7926,"t":"The Darkmoon Faire","lv":60,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Free Ticket Voucher to Gelvas Grimgate, located inside the Darkmoon Faire carnival.\nFree Ticket Voucher\nProvided: Free Ticket Voucher","desc":"The Darkmoon Faire is coming! Be sure to experience all the wonders and excitement of it when it comes to town!\nIf you act right now, you can redeem this voucher for free prize tickets! Just hand your voucher to Gelvas Grimgate located inside the carnival.\nRight now, the Faire is just outside Thunder Bluff, in Mulgore. Don't miss out! Go today!","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"Yes friend, may I help you? Do you have a voucher that needs redeeming?","done":"Welcome to the Darkmoon Faire! This voucher is good for FIVE, yes, FIVE prize tickets!\nWhen you accumulate prize tickets, you'll want to speak to me about redeeming them for valuable prizes. The more tickets you get, the more prizes you can win. Huzzah!\nOrgrimmar Mulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":49.4,"y":59.9,"n":"Kruban Darkblade","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.5,"y":68.9,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"6566":{"id":6566,"t":"What the Wind Carries","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Listen to Thrall.","desc":"It is good to see you again, ‹name›. The wind carries with it news from the Eastern Kingdom.\nSit, listen.","rew":"Experience: 650","back":"Patience, ‹name›. Pay attention!","done":"Are you prepared to take on this task?","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"95126":{"id":95126,"t":"The moonsilver blade","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Ott's Masterwork to Trevan Rol in Silverpine Forest.\nProvided: Ott's Masterwork","desc":"Here's the blade. You said that a paladin named Trevan sent you? Please extend my thanks to him for this opportunity when you next see him. Go with honor, friend.","rew":"You will receive:\nMoonsilver Blade\nExperience: 1,000","back":"Was Ott able to carry out the commission?","done":"<Trevan takes the blade and inspects it carefully.>\nThis will do nicely, Alteä. I knew that Ott had it in him to make something truly great.\nThe only thing left now is to kill that beast. Speak with Lumina when you are ready.\nHillsbrad Foothills Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":60.4,"y":26,"n":"Ott","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":41,"n":"Trevan Rol","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"4486":{"id":4486,"t":"The Tome of Nobility","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.","desc":"Well, well, well, look at the mighty paladin in all his/her regality.\nSorry, ‹name›, I meant no offense... I just get a little jealous sometimes when I see some of the feats you've accomplished. Tiza tells me it's my weakness, and I swore to her I'd work on it. It's just hard sometimes, you know?\nBut the reason I wanted to talk to you was because Duthorian Rall in Stormwind sent word for you to meet him in the Cathedral of Light when you're ready. Sounded important. Sounded like something's going on.","rew":"Experience: 320\nDun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54.8,"y":22.1,"n":"Brandur Ironhammer","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"246":{"id":246,"t":"Assessing the Threat","lv":17,"min":11,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Redridge Mongrels and 6 Redridge Poachers, then report back to Deputy Feldon in Lakeshire.\nRedridge Mongrel slain : 0/ 10\nRedridge Poacher slain : 0/ 6","desc":"We don't have men to spare, but something must be done about those gnolls you reported to me.\nScout southern Redridge for gnolls. Harry them, kill those you can and report back to me with a count of their numbers and an assessment of the threat they present. You may find those gnolls camped all along the southern road of Redridge.\nDo this for the Stormwind Army, ‹name›, and you will be rewarded.","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 950\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Excuse me, ‹name›, but we have a lot to keep our hands tied here. If you have nothing to report, then I must put my mind to other matters.","done":"<Deputy Feldon listens to your report...>\nThere's a sizable force of gnolls encamped there, and from what you tell me they are tough ones. It must not have been easy for you to gather this intelligence.\nHere you are, ‹name›. We are grateful for your aid.\nAnd if you haven't already done so, speak with Marshal Marris and Magistrate Solomon within Lakeshire. Our situation grows ever more desperate - those two will have need of you I'm sure.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":25.6,"y":60,"n":"Deputy Feldon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"1526":{"id":1526,"t":"Call of Fire","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Defeat the Minor Manifestation of Fire, and place the Glowing Ember in the brazier atop the Shrine of Eternal Flame.\nTorch of the Dormant Flame\nGlowing Ember Minor Manifestation of Fire\nProvided: Torch of the Dormant Flame","desc":"The fire sapta is finished. The time has come for you to face the flame. Use the sapta at the shrine and head to the top of the mountain to face the manifestation there. He will not attack until you are ready, but he will realize you are able to see him.\nStrike him down swiftly, ‹name›, for he shall only grow in power the longer you take to slay him. Once he is defeated, place his glowing embers within the brazier and light the torch.","rew":"You will receive:\nTorch of the Eternal Flame\nExperience: 1,150","back":"The brazier stands about a third your height, and looks normal, save for the inscriptions along its smooth metal rails. The metal shows no signs of wear from the weather, and the bowl seated at the top of it feels cool to the touch.","done":"A white hot flame ignites within the bowl as you place the ember within. You can feel the magical effects of the sapta coursing through your body and the fire dances rhythmically before you.\nYou place the top of the torch within the basin, and it immediately catches on fire.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":38.6,"y":59,"n":"Telf Joolam","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":39,"y":58.2,"n":"Brazier of the Dormant Flame","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"1126":{"id":1126,"t":"Hive in the Tower","lv":57,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Scale the tower of Southwind Village and locate a means to stir the silithid hive into activity. Bring back anything unusual you may uncover when doing so to Layo Starstrike at the Valor's Rest graveyard of Silithus.\nEncrusted Silithid Object Hive'Ashi Ambusher","desc":"The hive needs to be addressed in Southwind Village, and I think I know a way to get at them. It's been my experience that the silithid hives are very sensitive to their environment; this explains their attacks when hearing the death wails of the spirits.\nThe silithid are strongest in the tower - the one with the mass of wasps circling it. Scale the tower and jostle the hive into activity. Report back what you learn, but be careful! If you uncover anything that might help, bring it to me.","rew":"Experience: 6,000\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Well, did it work? You're still in one piece, which is good news. Did you find anything?","done":"What the... what is it?\nIt has the shape of a... box, maybe? It's encrusted over something fierce. Wait, there a portion here that's exposed... is that a book underneath all this gunk?\nI think you've stumbled across quite the find here, ‹name›... well, at least I hope it is. Perhaps it is a journal or a log from ancient times, preserved in this shell.\nI think I know a way to find out what this is.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":81.9,"y":18.9,"n":"Layo Starstrike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8806":{"id":8806,"t":"Grinding Stones for the Guard","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Dense Grinding Stones, 10 Solid Grinding Stones and 10 Heavy Grinding Stones to Vish Kozus, Captain of the Guard at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing III in order to complete this quest.\n10 Dense Grinding Stone\n10 Solid Grinding Stone\n10 Heavy Grinding Stone\nLogistics Task Briefing III\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing III","desc":"The Cenarion Hold guard is in short supply of grinding stones. Procure a batch and deliver them immediately to Captain Vish Kozus in Cenarion Hold.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":50.8,"y":33.7,"n":"Vish Kozus","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8246":{"id":8246,"t":"Signets of the Zandalar","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"15 Zandalar Honor Token\nReach 42000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nZandalar Signet of Might Zandalar Signet of Mojo Zandalar Signet of Serenity","back":"‹name› - for someone as exalted among the Zandalar as you are, I have something very special for you. Direct from our home in the South Seas... the Signets of the Zandalar! These signets are used to enhance any shoulder item you may possess. Should you seek might, mojo, or serenity - I have what you need!\nI ask for fifteen Zandalar Honor Tokens in exchange for your choice of one signet. If you have the tokens ready, then I'm ready to make a deal!","done":"A fair trade, my friend - please accept your signet with the blessing of the tribe!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.1,"y":16,"n":"Rin'wosho the Trader","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"3446":{"id":3446,"t":"Into the Depths","lv":51,"min":46,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Altar of Hakkar in the Sunken Temple in Swamp of Sorrows.\nAtal'ai Stone Circle\nProvided: Atal'ai Stone Circle","desc":"Inside the temple, I found a circular room with six balconies, each one with a serpent statue on the edge. Curious, I pushed one of them to see what would happen, and it was a trap! I nearly fell to my death from the explosion. Laying there on the ledge, I looked down and noticed that there was another statue at the base of the room; an altar of sorts... Hakkar, I think it was called.\nI think that this altar is the secret -- you must bring this token to the altar in the Sunken Temple.","rew":"Experience: 4,900","back":"Upon examining the statue, you notice a depression in its side, just the size of the token that Marvon gave you...","done":"You push the stone circle into the opening, and you hear it lock into place.\nNow that the stone is in place, you may continue... but what should you do next?\nPerhaps you should examine this altar further...","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.7,"y":45.9,"n":"Marvon Rivetseeker","s":1}],"cats":["sunken-temple"]},"1446":{"id":1446,"t":"Jammal'an the Prophet","lv":53,"min":38,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"The Atal'ai Exile in The Hinterlands wants the Head of Jammal'an.\nHead of Jammal'an Jammal'an the Prophet","desc":"My Witherbark companions don't take kindly to strangers around their home.\nMe? I don't have a home anymore. I was exiled from my people, the great Atal'ai tribe of the Swamp of Sorrows.\nOur spiritual leader, Jammal'an, had what he called a prophecy. He believes the summoning of the god, Hakkar will bring the Atal'ai immortality.\nBut I urged caution. What if the prophecy was nothing more than manipulation?\nI want revenge for my exile. Bring me Jammal'an's head. Maybe then my people will be free.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRainstrider Leggings Helm of Exile\nExperience: 6,550","back":"Once Jammal'an has been removed, I stand a chance of returning to my people.\nWith Jammal'an as their spiritual leader, the Atal'ai face certain destruction.","done":"Jammal'an's reckless trust of false visions led my people to their eternal doom.\nI thank you, ‹class›, for avenging my exile. I mourn for my people. I have no home to return to.\nThe Hinterlands Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":33.8,"y":75.2,"n":"Atal'ai Exile","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["sunken-temple"]},"99046":{"id":99046,"t":"The lost runner","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Search for Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow on the road leading to the Oracle Glade.","desc":"The Council of the Forest sent a small group of sentinels to the Oracle Tree some time ago. The tree sends messages to our elders, and it falls to us to deliver them to Darnassus safely.\nI received word that our most recent runner has not yet arrived. The Oracle's messages vary in frequency, but it has been abnormally long.\nPlease head towards the Oracle Glade along the road to to the west and check on her. It would have been Eralya Leafshadow's turn, and she is still in training. Elune guide you.","done":"Elune's grace... I shall not die... alone...","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56,"y":59.4,"n":"Sentinel Kyra Starsong","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":37.6,"y":36.8,"n":"Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"486":{"id":486,"t":"Ursal the Mauler","lv":12,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Ursal the Mauler and return to Athridas Bearmantle in Dolanaar.\nUrsal the Mauler slain","desc":"Now the time has come to save the Druids of the Talon. If we fail now, ‹name›, they will be forever lost in sleep.\nI shall prepare the Relics of Wakening and perform the ritual. For my work to take effect, the cursed beast responsible for this horrible situation must be slain. Only then will the ritual be complete.\nIt was Ursal the Mauler who meddled with our brethren's calling and it is Ursal the Mauler who must now pay so they can be freed. Travel to Gnarlpine Hold in the southwest and slay him.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDefender Axe Thornroot Club\nExperience: 1,150\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Our brethren cannot be awakened until Ursal the Mauler has been slain, ‹name›.","done":"‹name› you have proven yourself a most worthy and able ‹class›. A night elf who follows the path of honor as sure as you do is certain to find great glory in this world.\nMay the forest spirits protect you wherever your travels may take you.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56,"y":57.3,"n":"Athridas Bearmantle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"886":{"id":886,"t":"The Barrens Oases","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 85 experience instead of 90, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads.","desc":"The druids of Thunder Bluff sense a strange power leaking into the Barrens, east of Mulgore.\nTonga Runetotem was sent to discover the source of this power, but we fear he will need aid.\nTravel to the Barrens and speak with Tonga. He will be at the Crossroads. To reach there, take the road east out of Bloodhoof village. Enter the Barrens, then turn north when the road forks. Continue north and you will find the Crossroads.\nAnd do not leave the road, ‹name›, for the Barrens is a harsh land.","rew":"Experience: 85\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"My brethren in Thunder Bluff were wise to send you, young ‹class›. For the mystery of the Barrens is one that I alone cannot unravel.\nWith your aid, let us hope we can find answers to our questions.\nThunder Bluff The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":78.6,"y":28.6,"n":"Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.3,"y":31.9,"n":"Tonga Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"5046":{"id":5046,"t":"Razorhide","lv":20,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Blood Shard Bristleback Geomancer 49 % , Bristleback Thornweaver 48.8 % , Bristleback Water Seeker 48.7 % , Bristleback Hunter 34 % and 4 more","rew":"You will learn: Razorhide","back":"All those who <snort> enter battle have need of protection. Their bones must be strong. Their skin tough. <snort> My tribe knows this as well, and to add to the natural protection our quills and hide give us, <snort> we often call upon Agamaggan to protect us from harm before we go to war.\nBring me 4 blood shards <snort> and I will grant you the same protection.","done":"Go to war, ‹race›.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.5,"y":59.3,"n":"Mangletooth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"166":{"id":166,"t":"The Defias Brotherhood","lv":22,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,200 experience instead of 2,600, 2.38 times as much. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Kill Edwin VanCleef and bring his head to Gryan Stoutmantle.\nHead of VanCleef Edwin VanCleef in The Deadmines","desc":"There is but one task left for you to complete. Edwin VanCleef must be assassinated. While it saddens me to condemn any man to a death sentence, it is for the greater good of the people of Westfall that VanCleef is laid to rest once and for all. Bring me the villain's head once the deed is done.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nChausses of Westfall Tunic of Westfall Staff of Westfall\nExperience: 6,200\n+200 reputation with Stormwind","back":"How goes the hunt for Edwin VanCleef?","done":"‹name›, your bravery is remarkable. The People's Militia thanks you for your service to the people of Westfall. With VanCleef dead, this marks the beginning of the end for the Defias Brotherhood. Hopefully some day soon peace will once again grace the plains of this fair land.\nI salute you, Lord/Lady!","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56.3,"y":47.5,"n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-deadmines"]},"7846":{"id":7846,"t":"Recover the Key!","lv":51,"min":46,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Elder Torntusk at Jintha'alor wants you to kill Hitah'ya the Keeper to get the Shackle Key to his bindings. Return to Elder Torntusk when you have recovered the key.\nShackle Key Hitah'ya the Keeper","desc":"The key to my bindings is held by Hitah'ya the Keeper. She is in the nearby cave. Be careful, ‹class›, for she is guarded well.\nKill her and bring the key back to loosen my shackles. Only then will I be free to return home.","rew":"Experience: 6,100\n+200 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"You must hurry!","done":"Freedom at last! Thank you, ‹name›. Revantusk will know your deeds!\nThe Hinterlands Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":59.7,"y":77.8,"n":"Elder Torntusk","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"4966":{"id":4966,"t":"Protect Kanati Greycloud","lv":28,"min":23,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Protect Kanati Greycloud from the centaur attack.","desc":"But, there may be more centaur than I thought, I ask you, ‹name›, to fight with me against these vile assassins.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLightheel Boots Loamflake Bracers Palestrider Gloves\nExperience: 2,300\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Thank you for your help, ‹name›. I couldn't have held them off without you.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":21.3,"y":32.1,"n":"Kanati Greycloud","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"2966":{"id":2966,"t":"Seeing What Happens","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the miniature platinum discs to the gates of Uldum in Tanaris and look for clues as to the connection between the two.\nMiniature Platinum Discs\nProvided: Miniature Platinum Discs","desc":"Sage Truthseeker and I would like you to take the miniature discs you found to the sealed gates of Uldum. We... we aren't sure what will happen when you do this.\nThis sounds risky, sure, we acknowledge that. It might, however, do nothing. You might need to use the discs on something. Perhaps the doors unlock when you have the discs in your possession. Be open to try anything, and be ready for anything to happen.\nLearn what you can, then return to me. We will have much to discuss.","rew":"Experience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"This familiar looking pedestal sticks out of the hot sand. Perhaps there is something to its presence here...","done":"As you touch the pedestal, the miniature discs from Uldaman hum and glow in your backpack. A familiar feeling tingle washes over your hands, as the image of another Stone Watcher springs to life in front of the gates of Uldum.\n\"Salutations. I am a guardian of entry. The discs that have been used for access are missing the correct entry discs, the Plates of Uldum. Please incorporate these plates with the disc structure and repeat your access sequencing. Thank you.\"\nThunder Bluff Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":75.6,"y":31.6,"n":"Nara Wildmane","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":37.6,"y":81.4,"n":"Uldum Pedestal","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"3366":{"id":3366,"t":"The glowing shard","lv":25,"min":15,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Travel to Ratchet to find the meaning behind the Nightmare Shard.\nSpeak with someone about the Nightmare Shard\nProvided: Glowing Shard","desc":"The shard is a brilliant green, and although solid, what looks like smoke swirls just below the surface. You can't help staring into the depths of the crystal; at the same time, you know there is something very disturbing about it.\nMaybe you should see if anyone in Ratchet can tell you more about this strange shard.\nLevel 25 , requires level 15 Difficulty 15 21 23 28 33 Side Both factions Quest ID 3366","cats":["wailing-caverns"]},"1686":{"id":1686,"t":"The Shade of Elura","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 loads of Elunite Ore and the Medallion of Elura to Elanaria in Darnassus.\n8 Elunite Ore Crate of Elunite\nElura's Medallion Shade of Elura","desc":"You have learned much, ‹name›. Now we will craft you a weapon. A warrior's weapon.\nTo do this, you must travel to Darkshore.\nLong ago a ship crashed upon the rocks near the Auberdine lighthouse, scattering many crates of elunite ore along the ocean floor.\nFirst, you must defeat the elunite's guardian, the Shade of Elura. Once the ship's captain, she cursed herself to roam the deeps and protect her shipment for all time. Defeat her, gain her medallion, and gather the crates of lost Elunite.","rew":"Experience: 850","back":"Have you defeated the Shade of Elura, ‹name›? And do you have the lost elunite ore?","done":"Bravely done, ‹name›.\nYou have given the Shade of Elura much deserved peace, and we will use the gathered elunite to make a fine weapon for you.\nDarnassus Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":57.3,"y":34.6,"n":"Elanaria","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1846":{"id":1846,"t":"Dragonmaw Shinbones","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbones to Velora Nitely in the Undercity.\n8 Sturdy Dragonmaw Shinbone","desc":"To make the brutal leg guards, I need a brace of sturdy shinbones. The Dragonmaw orcs of the Wetlands have nice, thick shinbones. I'll need theirs.\nBut they must be sturdy. Be sure to test the shinbones as you collect them. If you can break them with your bare hands, then they won't be sturdy enough to work with.","rew":"Experience: 1,200","back":"I'm waiting for those shinbones, ‹name›. They'll make a nice frame for your leg guards.","done":"Well done! These all look strong. I think they'll do quite nicely. How did those orcs mind you taking their shins, ‹name›? Complain much?\nThat was another joke. You're not laughing.\nI'm not very funny these days, am I...","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":62.1,"y":39.1,"n":"Velora Nitely","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8406":{"id":8406,"t":"Fight for Warsong Gulch","lv":49,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The Silverwing Sentinels are at war with the Warsong Outriders due to the destruction the Orcs are causing to the forest. There are, however, more reasons to defend this particular forest than plain love for nature.\nThe forest forms a strategic barrier that makes Ashenvale defendable against a large-scale attack. Without it, Astranaar would last a day or two before being annexed to the Barrens.\nDo your part in fighting the Warsong Outriders, ‹name›! For the Alliance!","rew":"Experience: 2,250\n+50 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","back":"You've come back with news from the front, ‹name›?","done":"Good work, ‹name›. Thanks to you, our natural defenses in Ashenvale will remain intact for another day.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"98246":{"id":98246,"t":"Trying times","lv":29,"min":21,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Gather 12 Perfect Razormaw Eggs for Howin Kindfeather.\n12 Perfect Razormaw Egg","desc":"I'll need some eggs if my plan is going tae work. Bassbeak needs a nice an' full belly--I ain't in the business of hoppin' on the back of a surly gryphon.\nThey need to be perfect--no cracks or anything.\nTake some from the Razormaw raptors--they're known for having yolks the size of a gnome's noggin. You can find 'em in Raptor Ridge to the northeast and Saltspray Glen to the northwest.\nLet's make it a nice even dozen, just to be safe.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.4,"y":42,"n":"Howin Kindfeather","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"4806":{"id":4806,"t":"Frostmaul E'ko","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Frostmaul E'ko Frostmaul Preserver 20 % , Frostmaul Giant 20 %","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Juju Might","back":"In Winterspring, you have fought da large ice giants called frostmaul. Sheer power and force is at their disposal. If you wish ta gain da force of da frostmaul, bring me da E'ko you find from dem.\nRememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.","done":"Mau'ari can derive da juju for ‹name›... Use da Cache of Mau'ari to cast dis upon yourself or your allies.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Witch Doctor Mau'ari","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"5126":{"id":5126,"t":"Lorax's Tale","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Lorax. Listen to what he has to say.","desc":"The Satyr paces about and talks to himself. Do you wish to question him?","rew":"Experience: 650","back":"...","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":63.8,"y":73.8,"n":"Lorax","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"93926":{"id":93926,"t":"The western watch","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Peacekeeper Vaaniel at the western watchtower.\nCheck in on the Western Watchtower in the Shen'dar Highlands","desc":"Whatever reason the cult has for attacking the tower, it's not worth losing our people over.\nI'd like for you to head to the southwest and check in on that watchtower for us. Find the peacekeepers there and tell them to head back to the village. Holding that tower is not worth the lives it would cost and I'd rather concentrate the defenders we do have here to protect our citizens.\nPeacekeeper Vaaniel is in charge, let him know to head back here as quickly as possible. Hurry!","done":"<The body here is somewhat fresh, clearly only recently having been killed. Judging by the burns and scorch marks on this peacekeeper's skin, its clear that they were killed by the cult's storm-wielding spellcasters.>","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.6,"y":45.4,"n":"Constable Aonda","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42.4,"y":62,"n":"Peacekeeper Vaaniel","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"94486":{"id":94486,"t":"Feathers for binding","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 20 feathers from the Shadowgale Shrieklings in Shadowgale Forest.\n20 Pristine Shriekling Feather","desc":"The other ingredient I need for the poultice is feathers from the Shadowgale shrieklings that roam this forest. In their juvenile form, the shrieklings have insulative feathers which would be ideal to put over the moss. These feathers will prevent the antiseptic sap from drying out and will provide at least some protection against the elements.\nBe warned, the shrieklings are normally docile but they have been incredibly hostile of late. Their large talons can easily disembowel you if you aren't careful.","back":"It deeply saddens me to ask you to kill the young shrieklings, but with the rise in their aggression it is for the best. We can only handle so many emergencies at a time.","done":"Thank you for these. I will be sure to use every feather so their sacrifice will not be in vain.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":61.6,"y":39.2,"n":"Elegael Thornpaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92646":{"id":92646,"t":"Confront lorthuna","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Take the portal to the Rohashi Spires overhead and join Elaadrin Evengale and Ayessa Dawnsinger in their confrontation with the High Priestess Lorthuna.\nConfront Lorthuna","desc":"Lorthuna fled up to the spires above using some sort of portal. Ayessa and Elaadrin went in after her. That was just a few moments ago.\nI'm afraid I took one too many hits and this is where I stay. Go through the portal, find Ayessa and help them stop Lorthuna.\nUnless that help that Elaadrin and Ayessa said they sent for arrives soon, you are on your own from here. Good luck, ‹class›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBelt of Blades Empyrean Shoes Empyrean Greatsword Empyrean Treads\nMoney: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 460\n+100 reputation with Windshapers","done":"I sent a few of our healers to ensure that Valennia and her remaining forces made it back in one piece. She should be resting in the High Elder's residence now.\nMuln has already departed back to Azeroth, but he and I spoke of what is next for the Windshapers and our mission to Azeroth. Unfortunately, the island is more vulnerable than ever now and we need a plan to protect Zephras from what is to come.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":65.2,"y":50.4,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59,"y":79.6,"n":"Ayessa Dawnsinger","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});